backend-1   | │  **Join‑key mapping (explicit pairs)**                                       │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  | Left table & column                | Right table & column                 │
backend-1   | │  |                                                                           │
backend-1   | │  |------------------------------------|------------------------------------  │
backend-1   | │  -|                                                                          │
backend-1   | │  | `dev_film.film_id`                 → `dev_film_category.film_id` |        │
backend-1   | │  | `dev_film_category.category_id`    → `dev_category.category_id` |         │
backend-1   | │  | `dev_film.film_id`                 → `dev_inventory.film_id` |            │
backend-1   | │  | `dev_inventory.inventory_id`       → `dev_rental.inventory_id` |          │
backend-1   | │  | `dev_rental.rental_id`             → `dev_payment.rental_id` |            │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  **Explanation**                                                             │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  * `dev_film` is the central fact (film entity) containing the               │
backend-1   | │  **age‑rating** column (`rating`).                                           │
backend-1   | │  * `dev_film_category` links a film to one or more **genres**                │
backend-1   | │  (`category_id`).                                                            │
backend-1   | │  * `dev_category` holds the readable genre name (`name`).                    │
backend-1   | │  * `dev_inventory` ties each physical copy (inventory) to its film           │
backend-1   | │  (`film_id`).                                                                │
backend-1   | │  * `dev_rental` records every rental (view) of an inventory item             │
backend-1   | │  (`inventory_id`).                                                           │
backend-1   | │  * `dev_payment` records the monetary amount paid for a rental               │
backend-1   | │  (`rental_id`, `amount`).                                                    │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  These five join pairs create a complete path from the revenue/ view fact    │
backend-1   | │  (`dev_payment` / `dev_rental`) back to the film’s age rating and genre,     │
backend-1   | │  allowing the required aggregation.                                          │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
