backend-1   | │  **SQL Execution Plan – ClickHouse**                                         │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  **Goal** – Return, for every **age‑rating** (`dev_film.rating`) and         │
backend-1   | │  **genre** (`dev_category.name`), the **total revenue** and the **total      │
backend-1   | │  number of views** (rentals).                                                │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  ---                                                                         │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  ### 1. Source tables & verified columns                                     │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  | Table | Verified columns (used) | Source / verification |                 │
backend-1   | │  |-------|------------------------|-----------------------|                  │
backend-1   | │  | `dev_film` | `film_id`, `rating` | `get_clickhouse_schema` – film entity  │
backend-1   | │  & age‑rating |                                                              │
backend-1   | │  | `dev_film_category` | `film_id`, `category_id` | join‑bridge (film ↔      │
backend-1   | │  genre) |                                                                    │
backend-1   | │  | `dev_category` | `category_id`, `name` | genre name |                     │
backend-1   | │  | `dev_inventory` | `inventory_id`, `film_id` | physical copy of a film |   │
backend-1   | │  | `dev_rental` | `rental_id`, `inventory_id` | each rental = one view |     │
backend-1   | │  | `dev_payment` (or its monthly partitions) | `rental_id`, `amount` |       │
backend-1   | │  monetary amount per rental |                                                │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  All columns above are present in the confirmed schema; no invention is      │
backend-1   | │  required.                                                                   │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
